[medium] `lv_xml.h` appears twice in the include list — once before `#if LV_USE_XML` and once right after it. The duplication seems unnecessary and could be dropped to avoid confusion and reduce compile overhead. If the first include exists to make the `LV_USE_XML` macro visible, keep that one and remove the second.

```suggestion
#include "lv_xml.h"
#if LV_USE_XML

#include "lv_xml_base_types.h"
```
